{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>You shall not round the edge of your head.</b> This is one who makes his temples even with the back of the ear and the jaw, so that the edge of his head is found round all around — for at the back of his ears the roots of his hair are much higher than at his temples." "<b>The edge of your beard.</b> The end of the beard and its borders (Makkot 20a) — and they are five: two on each cheek, above by the head where it is broad, and it has two edges, and one below at the chin — the place where the two cheeks join together (Shevuot 50a)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:18.033479431Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}